      "evidence": "Citrea block 13496501 (0x1430d7dba56a5d5d8fb55680ef4a33465466fcfe0a39b92750664409be31f608), pinned eth_call/eth_getCode and runtime-matched CitreaScan verified source. D30 verdict: V1 fails (registry downstream closure partial); V2 fails (accepted unbounded paths have no new admission delay; eight genesis admissions had no veto window; initialize remains reachable after an insolvency-gated share wipe and zero token supply); V3 fails (200-bps holding-period voting is proven, but insolvency-gated-restructure is currently reachable below 1000 JUSD equity); V4 fails (all accepted minter execution cannot be rooted in continuing Equity veto); V5 passes (active parameter-change veto selector targets the authored JUSD controller); V6 fails closed (authorization census reconstructed, but capacity/code closure missing for five active minters); V7 fails for loss-interest issuance (fixed position rates cannot be minority-counter-proposed and elapsed interest is not capped at expiration). No D30 or D29 fallback credit is authored. Registry and Equity bytecodes match verified deployed source exactly. Savings has a 7-day qualified-holder overwriteable rate proposal with uint24 maximum 16777215 PPM (1677.7215% annually) and current/next zero rates; its earned interest is capped at available equity, so that payout is not native shortfall issuance. Position interest is usable principal times fixedAnnualRatePPM times elapsed time over 365 days; fixedAnnualRatePPM is uint24 with maximum successfully installed total 16777215 PPM (checked addition above that reverts), is only resynchronized on borrower mint, and _calculateInterest does not clamp time to expiration. Hub/position coverLoss can mint reserve shortfalls before principal burns and interest collection, so this path stays unbounded under D30-S rather than being relabeled raiseable/bounded. Reconciliation remains unknown: no newly obtained recurring whole-supply reconciliation establishes continuous/periodic coverage. Prior 2026-08-15 shutdown-notice research is historical evidence, not a refreshed active-incident or recovery verdict; the formerly official domain now resolves to a sale listing. Bridge-route data is untouched.",
